---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../../config/site';
const toc = [
  { id: 'what', label: 'What the integration does' },
  { id: 'requirements', label: 'What you need' },
  { id: 'connect', label: 'How to connect' },
  { id: 'window', label: 'The 24-hour window' },
  { id: 'disconnect', label: 'How to disconnect' },
  { id: 'permissions', label: 'Permissions' },
  { id: 'data', label: 'How your data is handled' },
];
---

<Legal
  title="WhatsApp integration"
  description={`How ${site.name} connects a WhatsApp Business number through Meta's Cloud API, what you need, the 24-hour messaging window, permissions and how to disconnect.`}
  intro={`Connect a WhatsApp Business number through Meta’s official Cloud API. Customer chats arrive in your ${site.name} inbox and your team and AI answer them together.`}
  eyebrow="Integrations · Messaging channel"
  badge="Live"
  toc={toc}
  dated={false}
>
  <h2 id="what">What the integration does</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Shows WhatsApp conversations with your business number in the shared inbox, with status, assignment, notes and full history.</li>
    <li>Sends the replies that you, your teammates or the AI write, with delivery receipts.</li>
    <li>Sends approved message templates when you need to reach a customer outside the 24-hour window.</li>
    <li>Feeds the same routing, SLA, escalation and reporting tools as every other channel.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The Official API needs no phone kept online and no QR code. {site.name} uses only the WhatsApp Business Account and numbers you choose.
  </p>

  <h2 id="requirements">What you need</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A Meta Business account and a WhatsApp Business Account (you can create one while connecting).</li>
    <li>A phone number that can receive a verification code and is not already registered on another WhatsApp app.</li>
    <li>Admin access to that business in Meta Business Suite.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="connect">How to connect</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Sign in to {site.name} at <a href={site.appUrl}>app.chithii.com</a> and open <strong>Settings → Messaging channels</strong>.</li>
    <li>Choose <strong>WhatsApp (Official API)</strong>. You are taken to Meta to log in.</li>
    <li>Pick or create your WhatsApp Business Account, add the number and verify it.</li>
    <li>Return to {site.name}. New messages to that number start appearing in your inbox.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="window">The 24-hour window and templates</h2>
  <p>
    WhatsApp lets a business reply freely for 24 hours after the customer’s last message. After that, only message templates approved by Meta
    can be sent. {site.name} shows when a conversation is outside the window and offers your approved templates. Meta may charge for some
    conversations under its own pricing; those charges are between your business and Meta.
  </p>

  <h2 id="disconnect">How to disconnect or revoke access</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>In {site.name}:</strong> open Settings → Messaging channels and disconnect the number. New messages stop arriving straight away.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>In Meta Business Suite:</strong> remove {site.name} from the apps connected to your business or WhatsApp Business Account.
      This revokes the access you granted, even if you can no longer sign in to {site.name}.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>What happens to messages already stored after you disconnect is described on the <a href="/data-deletion">data deletion page</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="permissions">Permissions {site.name} asks for</h2>
  <table>
    <caption class="sr-only">Permissions {site.name} requests</caption>
    <thead>
      <tr><th scope="col">Permission</th><th scope="col">Why {site.name} needs it</th><th scope="col">What it allows</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>whatsapp_business_management</code></td><td>To find the WhatsApp Business Account and numbers you chose, and their approved templates.</td><td>Reading and managing settings and templates for that account.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>whatsapp_business_messaging</code></td><td>To show messages sent to your number and send the replies you or the AI write.</td><td>Reading and sending WhatsApp messages for that number.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 id="data">How your data is handled</h2>
  <p>
    {site.name} uses messages, phone numbers, profile names and attachments from your connected number only to show conversations to your
    team, to generate suggested or automatic replies, and to send replies back. The <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains what is
    stored, who processes it and for how long.
  </p>
</Legal>
